  "notes": "Godan verb (さ row): {熟|じゅく}す・{熟|じゅく}します\nて-form: {熟|じゅく}して\nた-form: {熟|じゅく}した\n\nAlso read as {熟|う}れる (ichidan verb), which is more common for the literal ripening of fruit.\n\nKEY EXPRESSION:\n{機|き}が{熟|じゅく}す — \"The time is ripe.\" A very common set phrase meaning the right moment has arrived.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {果実|かじつ}が{熟|じゅく}す (fruit ripens)\n- {機|き}が{熟|じゅく}す (the time is ripe)\n- {議論|ぎろん}が{熟|じゅく}す (the discussion matures)\n- {計画|けいかく}が{熟|じゅく}す (a plan comes to fruition)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {熟|う}れる: The native Japanese reading, specifically for fruit ripening. More colloquial than {熟|じゅく}す.\n- {成熟|せいじゅく}する: To mature — more formal, used for people, societies, or markets reaching maturity.",
